# Copy this file to jdk.path (same folder). Put exactly ONE line: the JDK root folder that contains bin\java.exe
# (Android Studio's bundled runtime is usually named "jbr"; a standalone JDK is often jdk-21, jdk-17, etc.).
#
# In Android Studio: File -> Settings -> Build, Execution, Deployment -> Build Tools -> Gradle -> Gradle JDK
# Pick "jbr-21" (or similar) -> click folder icon to see path, or use Help -> About -> Copy path.
#
# Example (your path will differ):
# F:\Android\Android Studio\jbr
#
# If you only installed Java 26+, Gradle will fail ("Unsupported class file major version 70").
# Install JDK 21 LTS and point jdk.path or JAVA_HOME to that folder (not jdk-26).
